+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+## Contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` rejects input that violates a tool's declared schema by returning a `ToolResponse`, naming the failing property and constraint, and never invoking the executor ([validated by: rejects missing required input before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L10)).
+- A wrong-typed input is rejected without including the offending value in the returned message ([validated by: rejects wrong-typed input without leaking its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L28)).
+- Valid input, including unlisted extra properties, reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once.
+- An uncompilable static schema fails during registration and identifies the tool ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable schema at registration time](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
+- A function-valued tool definition is resolved and validated against the schema returned for the current call ([validated by: validates function-valued definitions against the current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L52)).
diff --git a/src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts b/src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts
